===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dóru}}From {{inh|en|enm|tre}}, {{m|enm|tree}}, {{m|enm|treo}}, {{m|enm|treou}}, {{m|enm|trew}}, {{m|enm|trow}}, from {{inh|en|ang|trēo}}, {{m|ang|trēow|t=tree, wood, timber, beam, log, stake, stick, grove, cross, rood}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*treu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*trewą|t=tree, wood}}, from pre-Germanic {{m|ine-pro|*dréwom}}, thematic e-grade derivative of {{inh|en|ine-pro|*dóru|t=tree}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates}}From the same Proto-Indo-European: {{cog|sco|tree|t=wood, rod, stick}}, {{cog|frr|tre}}, {{m|frr|trä|t=tree}}, {{cog|dum|tree}} > {{cog|nl|teer|t=tree}}, {{cog|da|træ|t=tree}}, {{cog|sv|trä|t=wood}}, {{m|sv|träd|t=tree}}, {{cog|no|tre|t=tree}}, {{cog|is|tré|t=tree}}, {{cog|got|𐍄𐍂𐌹𐌿|t=tree, wood, piece of wood}}, {{cog|sa|दारु|t=tree, wood}}, {{cog|sq|dru|t=tree, wood}}, {{cog|cy|dâr|t=oaks}}, {{cog|grc|δόρυ|t=wood, spear}}, {{cog|ru|де́рево}} or {{m|ru|дре́во}}, {{cog|xto|or}}. Related to {{m|en|tar}}, {{m|en|true}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

